  "live_records": {
    "q-46495": {
      "dom_id": "step-q46495",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Factor $36{a}^{6}+{b}^{8}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the given expression is a sum of squares, since\n\n$$\n36{a}^{6}+{b}^{8}={(6{a}^{3})}^{2}+{({b}^{4})}^{2}.\n$$\n\nTo factor a sum of squares, we first write it as a difference. Then, we rewrite the second term using ${\\text{i}}^{2}=-1.$ Finally, we factor as a difference of squares.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}36{a}^{6}+{b}^{8} & =36{a}^{6}-(-{b}^{8}) \\\\  & =36{a}^{6}-({\\text{i}}^{2}{b}^{8}) \\\\  & ={(6{a}^{3})}^{2}-{(\\text{i}{b}^{4})}^{2} \\\\  & =(6{a}^{3}+\\text{i}{b}^{4})(6{a}^{3}-\\text{i}{b}^{4})\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
